1. f4 d5 2. e4 dxe4 3. Nc3 Nf6
4. g4? { Threatens g5 to kick the knight, but it opens White's king's side completely. } 4... Bxg4 { The bishop takes the pawn and attacks the queen, so White has no time to win e4 back. }
5. Be2 Bf5 { The bishop steps back to guard the e4 pawn. Black is two pawns up and White's king's side is in ruins. } *
